{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560562-dark-ages-mage-pillars-for-akashayana-sahajoya-chakravante-etc","id":1560562,"title":"Dark Ages Mage: Pillars for Akashayana, Sahajoya, Chakravante, etc?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-11T18:20:14-07:00","id":1560562,"title":"Dark Ages Mage: Pillars for Akashayana, Sahajoya, Chakravante, etc?","content":"I adore Dark Ages Mage, and one of my fantasy projects has been to write Pillars for each of the proto-Traditions (who would be Fellowships in 1230 CE). I sneakily want to use Pillar and Foundation rules for a modern version as I love the DA: Mage magic system. Has anyone done work in this direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T20:53:45-07:00","id":1560563,"title":"","content":"While you may want to do something different, as the rules are a bit bare-bones and intended for a twisted offshoot of the Chakravanti, there are rules for the Itarajana in the V20 book &quot;The Black Hand&quot; which use the system of Foundation and Pillars that you find in DA: Mage, IIRC. It could at least help to provide some inspiration on that front. I'm not particularly familiar with the rules of DA: Mage, so I can't really comment on the comparative quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T21:34:56-07:00","id":1560566,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1494476-foundations-and-pillars-that-didn-t-appear?p=1495205#post1495205\">This post</a> has a copy of form Mage creative Malcolm Shephard's personal take on these for the Chakravanti and the Akashayana.<br /> <br /> As noted in the thread, there's also a technically official version for the Chakravanti in the V20: The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'mahe'Ra. The Solificati were a founding Tradition, but I think most people consider them close enough to the Hermetics that you can use the Order with their alternate Pillar instead of making your own. That leaves the Sahajiya as the odd ones out from official or pro-doing-fan-work level approaches. <br /> <br /> I'm sure someone has done either a Sahajiya or Seers of Cronus version on here. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> might know if hasn't done so already","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T16:00:58-07:00","id":1560658,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't be too hard to handle the Solificati kind of like the Craftmasons, as an offshoot of the Order of Hermes that replaces one of its Pillars with Materia. If I were to go that route, I'd differentiate them from the Craftmasons by which Pillar they allow to fall by the wayside: instead of Primus (Prime), I'd have them drop either Vires (Forces) or Corona (Mind).<br /> <br /> But to me, that would be a missed opportunity. Instead, I'd break out <b>Promethean: the Created</b> books, and draw from them inspiration for a Foundation and Pillars for the Solificati. The Foundation would be a sort of blend of Azoth and Pilgrimage, a quest for perfection; and the Pillars would be the four elements (Air, Earth, Fire, and Water), but largely metaphorical rather than literal, with Effects do for manipulating the body and mind as well as inanimate matter. Possibly align the levels (from the second to fifth dots) to align with the four-colored processes: Blackening, Whitening, Yellowing, and Reddening, with the first dot being detection as normal. <br /> <br /> On the Sahajiya, I unfortunately don't know of anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}